          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A child is identified as having intellectual disability only after starting scho</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A child is identified as having intellectual disability only after starting school, when academic demands exceed their ability. They communicate well, can read and write at a basic level, and are expected to live semi-independently as an adult. Which severity level best fits this presentation?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Moderate</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Moderate ID is usually identified earlier in childhood due to noticeable language and motor delays, and typically requires supported living arrangements as an adult.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Profound</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Profound intellectual disability presents with obvious delays from infancy, extremely limited communication, and requires lifelong intensive support.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Mild</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Mild ID accounts for approximately 85% of cases. These children often appear only mildly delayed before school and can develop basic literacy, social skills, and semi-independent adult living with some support.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Severe</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Severe ID is apparent from infancy with very limited expressive language and requires substantial lifelong support.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The key clues are late identification at school age, basic literacy, and expected semi-independent adult living — all characteristic of mild intellectual disability, which accounts for about 85% of cases."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct. Mild intellectual disability is the most common severity level and is often not recognised until school demands reveal the gap between ability and expectations."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
