          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A 5-year-old child is diagnosed with ADHD. The parents ask about starting medica</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A 5-year-old child is diagnosed with ADHD. The parents ask about starting medication immediately. What is the most appropriate first-line intervention at this age?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Start methylphenidate at a low dose and titrate upwards</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Methylphenidate is effective but is not first-line for children under six. Evidence-based guidelines recommend behavioural interventions first in this age group.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Referral for speech and language therapy</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Speech and language therapy is a core component of ASD management, not the first-line treatment for ADHD at any age.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Cognitive-behavioural therapy for the child</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>CBT requires a level of abstract thinking and self-reflection that is developmentally beyond most 5-year-olds. Structured behavioural strategies delivered through parents and caregivers are more appropriate.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Behavioural strategies and parent management training</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. For children under six, behavioural and educational strategies are the recommended first-line treatment, including consistent routines, immediate reinforcement, and structured parent management training programmes.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "For children under six with ADHD, behavioural strategies and parent management training are the recommended first-line treatment. Medication is reserved for school-age children with significant impairment despite behavioural interventions."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. Behavioural interventions are first-line for young children with ADHD. Medication becomes relevant for school-age children when behavioural strategies alone are insufficient."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
